y after complete source proof and actual no-publication determination. It is not a deserialized C candidate.\n-8. Recheck G/original/control/required cohort before returning the typed disposition. No new UTC, scheduler, source reduction or identity allocation in proof.\n+2. Bind and validate the actual existing G and authenticated original pair using the genuine original owner contract, including supported original version, tuple, hashes, source label and any admissionHistoryOrigin seed. Derive protocol obligations from THAT verified original/context before selecting a request/control route. A genuinely supported old/no-seed original may be LegacyEligible; a supported new seeded original requires its exact versioned history lifecycle. Missing, malformed, unsupported, foreign or unauthenticated original evidence cannot establish LegacyEligible. Missing seed is not itself proof of an old original if that original's version/owner contract requires one.\n+3. Read the actual request/control under the same source/lease closure. Its discriminator selects its parser ONLY; it cannot select, remove or upgrade the original's protocol obligations. For a LegacyEligible original, use unchanged legacy behavior only with a compatible old request/context (including absence only where the actual old owner allows it). A versioned control cannot upgrade that original or mint history authority. For a seeded original, require the supported matching versioned control and verify its exact seed/origin/G/tuple/original-hash binding before any dispatch, correlation, validation, cleanup or typed success.\n+4. Missing, unversioned, unknown-version, wrong-kind, malformed or foreign control with a seeded original is retained MissingOwnerProof or SourceConflict, never Legacy. Mixed modes in either direction and unknown modes retain evidence; same tuple does not repair the mismatch. Retirement is an exception only when the actual original/terminal/common owner independently proves the exact permitted settled disposition and evidence retirement. A missing file, terminal field, self-hash, Ready or apparent M3 alone is insufficient. Return the genuinely proved terminal/common disposition, not a legacy downgrade. Exact diagnostic choice remains part of R02; neither failure variant authorizes dispatch or deletion.\n+5. For a compatible versioned original/control pair, verify exact ordered transition grammar, current phase and source roles. Compare actual physical controls, Ready or worker task/proposal/outcome artifacts as applicable. Derive retries/merged canonical error applicability from actual rows and shared policy, never a serialized validated/no-previous-repair flag.\n+6. Recompute all PURE classification/freshness/comparison consequences from independently bound sources and recorded actual owner observations. Historical clocks/read failures are trusted named-owner observations within the existing trusted-local model; they are not claimed current metadata and hashes do not replace semantic verification.\n+7. Verify specialized restore/pending/worker/common owner relations. A parsed receipt with plausible fields is not a live reserve/take/release capability.\n+8. If full verified M3 exists, select its retained P0 path; do not repeat pre-P0 work. If control is admission_frozen and no attempted common debt exists, issue a distinct cold source-history capability only after complete source proof and actual no-publication determination. It is not a deserialized C candidate.\n+9. Recheck G/original/control/required cohort before returning ANY successful typed disposition, including Legacy. No new UTC, scheduler, source reduction or identity allocation in proof.\n+\n+The same original-selected matrix governs dispatch, correlation, validation, retention and cleanup in every consumer. It is not limited to this reader. A history-only control still never dispatches a GM request.\n+\n+| Authenticated original contract | Actual control | Permitted classification |\n+|---